menu "Sensing Network Config (TX)"

    config STA_SSID
        string "AP SSID to connect to (the RX's network)"
        default "wifi-sense-rx"
        help
            The transmitter is a station that connects to the receiver's AP.
            This must match the RX's AP_SSID. Override at runtime with the
            serial command STASSID: <name>.

    config STA_PASSWORD
        string "AP Password (match the RX)"
        default "wifi-sense-123"
        help
            Password for the sensing network. Must match the RX's AP_PASSWORD.

    config STA_CHANNEL
        int "AP WiFi Channel (0 = auto-scan)"
        default 0
        range 0 14
        help
            0 lets the station auto-scan for the SSID. Set it to the RX's
            AP_CHANNEL to skip scanning and bind faster.

    config PACKET_RATE
        int "Packet TX Rate (packets per second)"
        default "100"
        range 1 1000
        help
            The transmitter bursts UDP packets at this rate; the receiver
            produces one CSI record per packet. 0 means "as fast as possible"
            (soft-capped ~100 Hz by the OS delay). Serial command RATE: <n>
            changes this live.

    config SHOULD_COLLECT_CSI
        bool "Should this ESP32 collect and print CSI data?"
        default "n"
        help
            Keep OFF on the transmitter - CSI is only meaningful at the RX
            and collecting here halves the achievable sampling rate.

    config SEND_CSI_TO_SERIAL
        depends on SHOULD_COLLECT_CSI
        bool "Send CSI data to Serial"
        default "n"

endmenu